From b00154cc52754deadc83c374414fd66d530f1959 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 13:51:54 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: CCL (U2225) and a generic pad-to-peripheral input
 path

Pads as peripheral inputs: PORT gains "func-in"[pin * 16 + f], the pad's
level while the pin is muxed to function f (else 0), and the SoC wires
it to every model input named "pad-<group>-in"[n] from the device's
signal table, OR-ing the pads that carry one signal
(pic32cm_connect_pad_inputs()). The EIC keeps its own function-A path.

The CCL as PIC32CM MC00 silicon showed it (firmware/hello APP=cclprobe
and cclprobe2, checked by ccl):

- OUTn = TRUTH[IN2 IN1 IN0] with IN0 = IN[3n]; INSEL MASK, FEEDBACK
  (the pair's sequencer, 0 without one), LINK (LUT n + 1, LUT3 wraps to
  LUT0), EVENT (a strobe three GCLK_CCL edges after the input's edge),
  IO (the pads), AC (comparator n % count), TC/ALTTC (WO[0] of TCn,
  TCn+1), TCC (WO[x] of TCC(n % count); TCC1/TCC2 repeat CC0's output
  on WO[2]) and SERCOM (reads 1: idle).
- SYNCH passes a change at the second GCLK_CCL edge, FILTER at the
  fourth if it held; EDGESEL gives a one-cycle pulse on rising edges.
- DFF and JK sequencers change at clock edges (J = K = 1 toggles at half
  the clock), LATCH and RS at once; a disabled even LUT clears the
  sequencer; OUT2N is the sequencer, OUT2N+1 the odd LUT's own output.
- A disabled LUT or CCL drives its pad to 0; "lutout-event" is OUTn's
  level while LUTEO.
- LUTCTRLn's bits but ENABLE take a write only while CTRL.ENABLE is 0
  and the LUT was disabled before the write (stricter than the data
  sheet); SEQCTRL and RUNSTDBY only while the CCL is off (overlay).

The SoC taps TC WO[0], TCC WO[0..2] and AC CMPn for the CCL without
pads: pic32cm_connect_pads() adds the CCL as an extra sink of those
signals and ORs its "tap-*-active" lines into the sources'
"pad-wo-active", so they stop coasting while a LUT reads them.

qtest pic32cm-ccl-test: truth table, protection, LINK, filter edges,
DFF.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
